# Public storefront — shoppers, mostly signed out
#
# Copy to .env.local for development. `.env.local` is gitignored; this template
# is tracked on purpose so a fresh clone can see the contract.

# Origin of digistore-api. NO trailing slash.
# Local: the API defaults to port 4000 (see digistore-api/.env.example).
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Path prefix every API route mounts under. MUST match BASE_PATH on the API —
# it is a variable rather than a constant so the two cannot drift.
API_BASE_PATH=/api/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session (Part C — not used by the scaffold)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Under the BFF (ADR-0003) this app's route handlers hold the session cookie,
# so a secret for signing/encrypting it belongs here, NOT on the API.
#
# ⚠️ When that cookie is set, scope it to THIS EXACT SUBDOMAIN
# (shop.example.com) and never to `.example.com`. A parent-domain cookie is
# readable by all three apps and silently destroys the session separation that
# three subdomains exist to provide.
# SESSION_SECRET=
